 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 13260,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"8111\" data-start=\"7758\"><strong data-end=\"7771\" data-start=\"7760\">Answer Key:</strong></p>\n\n<ol data-end=\"2831\" data-start=\"2257\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2335\" data-start=\"2184\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4295\" data-start=\"4063\"><strong data-end=\"4095\" data-start=\"4079\">Cryptography</strong> encrypts files, network data, and system credentials to ensure data confidentiality and integrity. For example, Linux uses LUKS for full disk encryption; SSH uses encryption for secure remote logins.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2335\" data-start=\"2184\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4295\" data-start=\"4063\"><strong data-end=\"4320\" data-start=\"4297\">User authentication</strong> verifies user identity before granting system access. For instance, login credentials, biometric scanners, or smart cards prevent unauthorized logins.</p>\n\n\t<p data-end=\"4624\" data-start=\"4473\">Together, these mechanisms protect against data theft, unauthorized access, and ensure that only trusted users can access sensitive resources in an OS.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
